# Chopshop Studio — operator configuration.
#
# Copy to .env (gitignored) and edit. Nothing here names a host, a network or a
# machine: a runner is whatever URL you point at, so ONE file describes a
# single-box install and a split install equally well. That is deliberate — the
# repo must not learn anyone's topology.
#
#   podman run -d --name chopshop-app -p 127.0.0.1:3001:3001 \
#     -v "$PWD":/app:rw --env-file .env chopshop-app

# --- the app --------------------------------------------------------------
RAILS_ENV=development
SECRET_KEY_BASE=change-me
CHOPSHOP_PASSWORD=change-me

# --- runners --------------------------------------------------------------
# One variable per runner, keyed by the label you want to see in the GUI. The
# label is the variable name with CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_ and _URL stripped and
# lower-cased, so underscores stay underscores:
#
#   CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_STUDIO_A_URL   ->  "studio_a"
#
# A runner's KIND defaults to "svg": the pipeline contract (doc/runner-contract.md)
# — prep, trace, gate. Set _KIND=flux for a chopshop-flux service, which generates
# a raster from a prompt and speaks its own standard API instead. The svg default
# is why renaming a runner needs no code change anywhere.

# Shape 1 — LOCAL MONOLITH. Everything on one box.
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_SVG_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8791
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8795
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_KIND=flux

# ...unless the studio is itself in a container on that same box, which is the
# dev rig here. A container cannot reach a service bound to the HOST's loopback:
# measured, with the service on 127.0.0.1 the container gets ECONNREFUSED, and on
# 0.0.0.0 it gets 200. So for that shape, bind the service to 0.0.0.0 (or the
# bridge address) and point the studio at the host:
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_URL=http://host.containers.internal:8795
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_KIND=flux

# Shape 2 — SPLIT. The studio here, the compute elsewhere. Any address that
# reaches it: a tailnet name, a LAN address, a tunnel. Both ends need nothing
# from each other beyond the URL and the tokens below.
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_SVG_URL=http://pipeline-host:8791
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_URL=http://compute-host:8795
# CHOPSHOP_RUNNER_FLUX_KIND=flux

# Where a flux job hands its raster once it has been generated. Defaults to the
# first non-mock pipeline runner above, so it usually needs no setting.
# CHOPSHOP_FLUX_HANDOFF_RUNNER=svg

# --- tokens ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Bearer token between the studio and a pipeline runner, if that runner sets one.
# RUNNER_TOKEN=change-me

# The chopshop-flux service's OWN token. Separate from RUNNER_TOKEN on purpose:
# that service keeps a clean standard API which other applications also call, so
# it does not share the pipeline's credential.
# CHOPSHOP_FLUX_TOKEN=change-me
